## ABSTRACT
Sulfide compounds provide a type of promising alternative for oxygen evolution reaction (OER) electrocatalysts due to their diversity, intrinsic activities, low-price and earth-abundance. However, the unsmooth mass transport channel, the collapse of the structure and insufficient intrinsic activities limit their potential for OER performance. In respond, the dense Fe-doped \(\mathsf{C o}_{9}\mathsf{S}_{8}\) nanoparticles encapsulated by S, N co-incorporated carbon nanosheets (Fe/Co9S8@SNC) were proposed and synthesized via fast thermal treatment from ultrathin metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) nanosheets. In designed catalysts, the nanosheet configuration connected by nanoparticles retained rich access for permeation of electrolyte and precipitation of \(O_{2}\) bubbles during OER process. Meanwhile, the outer carbon layer of \(\mathsf{C o}_{9}\mathsf{S}_{8}\) provided additional catalytic activity while acting as armor to keep the structure stability. At the atomic scale, the doped Fe regulated the local charge density and the d-band center for facilitating desorption of oxygen intermediates. Benefiting from this multi-scale regulation strategy, the Fe- \(\mathsf{C o}_{9}\mathsf{S}_{8}\ @\mathsf{S N C}\) displays an ultralow overpotential of \(273\;\mathsf{m V}\) at \(10\;\mathsf{m A}\cdot\mathsf{c m}^{-2}\) and small Tafel slope of \(55.8\ m\lor\cdot\mathsf{d e c}^{-1}\) , which is even close to the benchmark \(\mathsf{R u O}_{2}\) catalyst. This concept could provide valuable insights into the design of other catalysts for OER and beyond.
## KEYWORDS
\(\mathsf{C o}_{9}\mathsf{S}_{8}\) , water oxidation, electronic structure, multi-scale regulation, d-band center
## 1 Introduction
The oxygen evolution reaction (OER) is a vital half-reaction involved in water electrolysis [1–3], rechargeable metal-air batteries and electro-synthesis [4–8], which plays a pivotal role to utilize the renewable energy source [9]. Among the investigated non-noble electrocatalysts for OER, sulfide compounds, especially Co-based sulfide compounds provide a type of promising alternative due to their diversity, low-price, and earth-abundance [10–12]. Considering the actual situation for industrial application, ideal Co-based sulfide compounds electro-catalysts for OER should possess smooth mass transport channel, stable structure and high intrinsic activities [13]. Therefore, remarkable efforts have been made to improve electro-catalytic oxygen evolution performance, such as, doping heteroatom [3, 14], loading on conductive substrate [15–17], building heterojunction [18, 19], and regulating morphology [10, 20]. However, to date, a promising Co-based sulfide compounds electro-catalyst simultaneous with sufficient intrinsic activities and smooth transport channel to exhibit excellent electrocatalytic performance is always interesting but challenging. Besides, sulfide compounds are easily decomposed during electro-oxidation process under alkaline conditions, which also limits the development of sulfide compounds with efficient water electro-oxidation properties [21, 22]. Therefore, an unanswered question critical to Co-based sulfide compounds is how to synergistically regulate the intrinsic activities, mass transport and structure stability on OER process.
